<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, maximum-scale=1.0, user-scalable=no">
    <title>Drop Cap Editor</title>
    <style>
        html, body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            height: 100%;
            overflow: hidden;
            font-family: "Georgia", serif; /* Serif fonts look best for drop caps */
            background-color: #ffffff;
        }
        
        .app-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            height: 100vh;
            height: -webkit-fill-available;
        }

        .editor-box {
            flex: 1;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 24px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.7;
            outline: none;
            overflow-y: auto;
            -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
        }

        /* TARGETS ONLY THE VERY FIRST PARAGRAPH */
        .editor-box p:first-of-type {
            text-indent: 0; /* No indent needed when a drop cap is present */
        }

        /* TARGETS THE FIRST LETTER OF THE FIRST PARAGRAPH */
        .editor-box p:first-of-type::first-letter {
            font-size: 55px;
            font-weight: bold;
            float: left;
            line-height: 42px;
            padding-top: 4px;
            padding-right: 8px;
            padding-left: 3px;
            color: #0071e3; /* Elegant blue accent color */
            font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
        }

        /* TARGETS ALL FOLLOW-UP PARAGRAPHS (Auto-Indentation) */
        .editor-box p ~ p {
            text-indent: 35px; 
            margin-top: 0;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .button-bar {
            padding: 12px 20px;
            background-color: #f5f5f7;
            border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e7;
        }

        button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 14px;
            background-color: #0071e3;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 8px;
            font-size: 16px;
            font-weight: 600;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="app-container">
        <div class="editor-box" contenteditable="true" id="myEditor">
            <p>Once upon a time, you decided to build your own full-screen writing tool. The first letter of this paragraph automatically converts into a beautiful drop cap layout as you type your text.</p>
            <p>This is the second paragraph. Notice how it ignores the drop cap rule and applies your standard auto-indentation layout instead, keeping your styling clean and orderly.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="button-bar">
            <button onclick="copyText()">Copy All Text</button>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function copyText() {
            var editor = document.getElementById("myEditor");
            navigator.clipboard.writeText(editor.innerText);
            
            var btn = document.querySelector("button");
            var originalText = btn.innerText;
            btn.innerText = "✓ Copied!";
            btn.style.backgroundColor = "#34c759";
            
            setTimeout(function() {
                btn.innerText = originalText;
                btn.style.backgroundColor = "#0071e3";
            }, 2000);
        }
    </script>

</body>
</html>
